# Job: node framework — ClientServer ready wait bounded by the call's own deadline (F-R5-9, D-108)

You are a codex sub-agent under a Claude supervisor. Model gpt-6-astra, reasoning xhigh. Cap 2 h. Read `AGENTS.md` (root) §2/§3/§4.1/§5, `framework/AGENTS.md` and the language AGENTS.md. Campaign rules (`doc/plan/c016-worklog/decisions.ko.md` D-098, D-101, D-105, D-107, D-108): one owner per rule, fewer rules, no mitigations (no timeouts/retries/second pollers/catch-alls), cross-language parity mandatory, regression test per fix, monotonic durations (D-095). Never modify `core/**`, `bindings/**`, any `doc/spec/**`, `framework/doc/**`, `doc/site/**`, other languages. Never lower an assertion. Do not commit — keep each cause in a separable diff and describe the split in the summary. Do not run sample runners (supervisor gate).

## Spec
`framework/doc/framework/common/spec/server/02-channel-transport/02-channel-messaging.ko.md` §3.2/§10 and
`03-spot-actor/04-actor-model.ko.md` §8.1 (deadline owner = the operation): a ClientServer call waits for a ready server at most
min(the call's remaining deadline, 5 s), counted from the call's submission, and the subsequent request gets only the remaining
time of that same deadline. Reference: dotnet `ZLinkClientServerClientRuntime.cs:232-251` (one `timeout`, `_time.GetTimestamp()`
at start, `remaining = timeout - elapsed`).

## Cause (verified)
`framework/languages/node/packages/framework/src/runtime/channels/channel-socket-registry.ts:664-667`
(`clientServerReadyWaitBoundMs`) bounds the ready wait by the channel/host default request timeout, not the call's timeout, and
`:1684-1692` then passes the whole original `timeoutMs` to `dealer.request`.

## What to do
Thread the call's deadline (monotonic, `performance.now()`) through the ready wait: bound = min(remaining, 5 s); pass the remaining
time to the request; a call whose deadline expires during the ready wait ends with the existing no-ready result. Remove the
channel-default lookup for this bound if nothing else uses it. Regression tests: short per-call timeout (e.g. 200 ms) with no ready
server ends within that timeout (monotonic assertion, not wall clock); a ready server that appears after 100 ms is used with the
remaining time; long timeout still caps the wait at 5 s.

